{"skill":{"slug":"youtube-transcript","displayName":"YouTube Transcript"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1769532361984,"changelog":"Initial public release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1352,"sha256":"f8843aca94abffecb456a7e71fef337bd814150f215a66f7733c373488b3d43a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/SETUP.md","size":2577,"sha256":"38ece2a1d31bfbc19c66f325c8a03da25d305e63d5767a9ec8f38b19bd531003","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/fetch_transcript.py","size":4640,"sha256":"185ac655f26ba8b600500dfa5df098a5a6d5435eba143b10623b1565106e9e5f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2294,"sha256":"1599084b9a44f7b4392f2aa34c70dad7b848c0a85ccb6bb76698e7fc3acbc5eb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022119508,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3394730743e4e63419e4fc08d7c9d7937bc2742b8557fa1a1ed4fc190b57c2cd","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3394730743e4e63419e4fc08d7c9d7937bc2742b8557fa1a1ed4fc190b57c2cd","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: youtube-transcript\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its use of `subprocess.run` in `scripts/fetch_transcript.py` to execute system commands like `wg-quick up` and `ip rule add`. These commands manage a WireGuard VPN interface and manipulate network routing, which typically requires elevated privileges and grants significant control over the host system's network configuration. While these actions are plausibly needed for the stated purpose of bypassing YouTube's cloud IP blocks, they represent a high-risk capability that could be abused if the agent's environment has broad permissions.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160136211},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":74,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789022119508},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This YouTube transcript skill is mostly transparent about its purpose, but it can change host VPN/routing settings and contact an extra metadata service, so it should be reviewed before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script binds transcript requests to a VPN source IP, but also automatically runs wg-quick and ip rule commands that can affect the shared host network namespace; it also sends the video ID to noembed.com through a normal requests.get call not routed through the VPN-bound session.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Setup instructs users to install unpinned Python packages and configure WireGuard under /etc/wireguard, including broad AllowedIPs routing through a residential endpoint, without strong warnings or dependency integrity controls.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Invocation is scoped to YouTube transcript, summary, or extraction requests rather than generic summarization, but it does not require explicit user confirmation before proxy/VPN-backed retrieval or automatic VPN setup.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No backdoor, service installation, cron job, memory poisoning, or credential exfiltration was found, but the WireGuard setup and added routing rule can persist or accumulate at the host networking level depending on system configuration and repeated runs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The transcript-fetching purpose is coherent, and residential VPN/proxy use is disclosed in the skill description and setup guide, but the implementation goes beyond content retrieval by attempting privileged WireGuard startup and host policy-route changes when the VPN is unavailable.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intentionally want transcript requests routed through a residential VPN/proxy and you are comfortable with host-level WireGuard and routing changes. Prefer running it as an unprivileged user in an isolated environment, preconfigure networking outside the skill, pin dependencies, and treat noembed.com as an additional party that can see requested video IDs.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Shell and network access are expected for this design, but the skill lacks explicit permission boundaries for privileged network commands and outbound destinations.\n[SQP-1] expected: The trigger text is YouTube-specific, so the broad-invocation concern is downgraded; however, user-directed confirmation would be appropriate because activation can lead to proxy/VPN use.\n[SQP-2] expected: Residential IP proxying is disclosed in SKILL.md, but the disclosure does not clearly require consent before using a policy-sensitive bypass path.\n[SQP-2] expected: The setup guide clearly instructs residential WireGuard routing, including 0.0.0.0/0 AllowedIPs, but does not adequately explain privacy, ISP, or home-network implications.\n[SQP-3] expected: The default language list is documented and user-overridable with a second argument, so this is not a material security concern.\n[AST4] expected: The wg show subprocess uses fixed arguments and no shell, so command injection was not supported by the artifact; it is expected for VPN status checking.\n[SDI-2] expected: VPN/routing operations are part of the stated design, but automatically altering host networking is high-impact and insufficiently controlled for a transcript skill.\n[AST4] expected: The wg-quick subprocess uses fixed arguments, but it can process host WireGuard configuration and make privileged system network changes without an explicit opt-in flag.\n[AST4] expected: The ip rule subprocess uses fixed arguments, but it mutates host routing state, ignores return codes, and has no cleanup or idempotency check.\n[T05] expected: The static finding is supported: bring_up_vpn automatically invokes wg-quick and adds a policy-routing rule if the VPN check fails.\n[T08] unexpected: The setup guide installs youtube-transcript-api and requests without pins, hashes, or a virtual environment recommendation; this is a supply-chain hygiene issue rather than evidence of malicious dependency use.\n[other] unexpected: The script sends each video ID to noembed.com for title and author lookup, and this third-party recipient is not documented in the skill instructions.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022119508}}}}}